<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Mod id="871da714-b2c6-49e9-8882-57489f501dbc" version="1">

  <Properties>
    <Name>(8)  Air Archive for VP</Name>
    <Teaser>Air Archive for VP (add Airunits )</Teaser>
    <Description>Wingline adds historical aircraft from the early biplane era up to the F-35. It expands Fighters and Bombers with a simple, AI-friendly concept that makes air warfare deeper without becoming micro-heavy.[NEWLINE]
New Air Units are woven into the existing tech tree as a dedicated line, upgrading at the same pace as vanilla to keep balance and compatibility.[NEWLINE]
[NEWLINE][COLOR_NEGATIVE_TEXT]To adjust aircraft animation speed (x1 by default), open[ENDCOLOR] Faster Aircraft Animations.sql [COLOR_NEGATIVE_TEXT]and follow the instructions.[ENDCOLOR][NEWLINE]
[NEWLINE]
[COLOR_CYAN]What’s inside:[ENDCOLOR][NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Expanded Fighter line (WWI → Jet Age → 5th Gen)[NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Expanded Bomber line (Light/Medium → Strategic → Modern Jet Bombers)[NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Seamless upgrade chain and AI-manageable costs/stats[NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Clean integration with vanilla/VP tech pacing[NEWLINE]
[NEWLINE]
[COLOR_CYAN]Credits (3D models / base assets):[ENDCOLOR][NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Biplanes / Early Monoplanes — (various classic authors)[NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Mid-century Jets (e.g., P-80, Mirage class) — (attributed where applicable)[NEWLINE]
[ICON_BULLET] Modern Airframes (e.g., MiG-29, B-52/B-1/Tu-95, F-35/Su-57 class) — (attributed where applicable)[NEWLINE]
[NEWLINE]
[COLOR_CYAN]More info:[ENDCOLOR] Wingline_Info.txt[NEWLINE]
[COLOR_CYAN]Homepage:[ENDCOLOR] (to be announced)
    </Description>
    <Authors>CAYM</Authors>
    <SpecialThanks>Asterix Rage o, civplayer33, jarcast2, Nutty, pineappledan</SpecialThanks>
